    "Diagnostic evidence only. The full original first declaration did not complete; no qualification or global counter increment is supported.",
    "The collector starts before human.admit. Portfolio25 also adds direct-canonical bookkeeping to the labelled diagnostic. These observations do not establish a causal performance comparison with Portfolio23 or earlier attempts.",
    "All bucket values are cumulative at an observed checkpoint. Inclusive durations overlap, are rounded to integer milliseconds, and must not be summed across bucket families into total CPU or wall time. Pending spans can be nested.",
    "The six canonical.digest surfaces partition the recorded digestSfValue invocation population; their counts and inclusive durations may be summed for that bucket name. Each invocation has one digest span. Labels identify direct labelled call sites, not complete ancestry, and unlabelled calls remain unattributed.",
    "canonical.direct measures direct canonicalSfValue calls outside active digest canonicalization; internal digest canonicalization is excluded. Neither canonical bucket measures all serialization, all canonical work outside the frame, or all CPU work.",
    "root.caller.* instruments PlannerCalculationServices only. It does not cover the direct Finance caller. Missing caller buckets do not imply that Root was unused or attribute every Root invocation to Finance.",
    "state.read.identity-absent aggregates read namespaces and arbitrary callbacks. It is not a count of missed selectSfCaseIdentity opportunities.",
    "The baseline-accessor rejection branch rejects an unsupported accessor before comparing getter/setter identities. That reason would not prove getter/setter equality. No such rejection bucket was observed in this prefix.",
